You can do the following in your own project to disable errors on bad content type.

```python
from flask.wrappers import Request

class AnyJsonRequest(Request):
    def on_json_loading_failed(self, e):
        if e is not None:
            return super().on_json_loading_failed(e)

app.request_class = AnyJsonRequest
```

The PR of the commit you linked describes why the change was made and how to adapt to it: https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/pull/2040 It is highly recommended to use aware datetimes if possible.

Otherwise, you can register a different tag for datetimes if you need different behavior in your application.

```python
from flask.json.tag import TagDateTime

class TagNaiveDateTime(TagDateTime):
    __slots__ = ()

    def to_python(self, value):
        return super().to_python(value).replace(tzinfo=None)

app.session_interface.serializer.register(TagNaiveDateTime, force=True)
```

