This is how I now analyze this problem.

The 404 is expected as only a match to a route would result in the blueprint before_request triggering (partial matches, e.g. to the prefix don't trigger anything). If you want to match any route that has the parents prefix you can use the path url convertor as a catch all e.g. 
```python
@child_bp.route("/<path:path>")
def all_child():
    ...
```

This is something you can add to your own code,
```python
def redifor(endpoint):
    return redirect(url_for(endpoint))
```
but it is not suitable for a library like Flask as it is much less clear what the function does. This is also likely true for your code - would you remember in a years time what `redifor` means?

